    "reason": "[ev-d1948f134793] says only that the TCP LoadBalancer `terminationDelay` option \"has been removed\" and can now be configured on `TCPServersTransport`. It does not say what happens to configurations that still set it: whether the value is ignored, rejected or still honoured. The CRD validator also refuted the removal: the v3.0.0 IngressRouteTCP schema [ev-f7d1f0ce407c] still contains spec.routes[].services[].terminationDelay, which contradicts the claim that the field \"will be ignored\" at the CRD level. To settle the consequence kind, we need evidence on how Traefik v3 handles a terminationDelay value set at the service level, such as release notes, code or provider documentation.",
